---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import AirportCodeLookup from '@/components/tools/reference/AirportCodeLookup.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="airport-code-lookup">
  <AirportCodeLookup client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to use the airport code lookup</h2>
    <p>
      Type a three-letter IATA code (LHR), a four-letter ICAO code (EGLL), a city or part of an airport
      name. The airport code lookup shows exact code matches first, then airports in a city with that
      name, then other names that contain your text, with large airports before small ones. Select a
      result to see its codes, country, type and position on the map.
    </p>
    <h2>IATA and ICAO codes</h2>
    <p>
      The International Air Transport Association gives three-letter codes to airports with passenger
      or cargo service; they appear on tickets, timetables and bag tags. The International Civil
      Aviation Organization gives four-letter codes for flight plans and air traffic control. The
      first letter of an ICAO code is the region: K for the contiguous United States, E for northern
      Europe, R for East Asia.
    </p>
    <h2>Data</h2>
    <p>
      The list comes from OurAirports, an open data set of airports in the public domain, and has
      every airport, seaplane base and heliport with an IATA code. The site refreshes it each month.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
